Rule 1 (input, tensor1 and tensor2 should have the same number of dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_3)
>>
Rule 2 (value should be an integer if the input tensors are integer types)
{v_1 : tensor, v_4 : int ⊎ float} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 5) then (v_4 = 0 ∨ v_4 = 1 ∨ v_4 = 2 ∨ v_4 = 3 ∨ v_4 = 4 ∨ v_4 = 5)
